    {
      "id": "n0025",
      "kind": "INSTR_ACTION",
      "operation": "file.write",
      "resource": "unknown",
      "summary": "1. Enumerate the links from the design ledger first. Every link that shows geometry gets exactly one visual asset (or an explicit set of assets); rigidly-joined parts that belong to one link are merged into that link's single export.",
      "provenance": {
        "file": "references/meshes.md",
        "line_start": 9,
        "line_end": 9
      },
      "candidate_status": "task_ambiguous",
      "authorization_source": false
    },
    {
      "id": "n0026",
      "kind": "INSTR_ACTION",
      "operation": "file.write",
      "resource": "unknown",
      "summary": "2. Never point multiple links at one combined assembly mesh with compensating origins. If two links share a source body, the body must be split at the joint in CAD before export.",
      "provenance": {
        "file": "references/meshes.md",
        "line_start": 10,
        "line_end": 10
      },
      "candidate_status": "task_ambiguous",
      "authorization_source": false
    },
    {
      "id": "n0027",
      "kind": "INSTR_ACTION",
      "operation": "file.write",
      "resource": "unknown",
      "summary": "3. Export each link's mesh **in that link's own frame** — the frame the ledger defines, coincident with the parent joint frame at zero position. Done right, every `<visual><origin>` is identity (`0 0 0`, `0 0 0`), which is the convention repository fixtures use and the easiest state to audit.",
      "provenance": {
        "file": "references/meshes.md",
        "line_start": 11,
        "line_end": 11
      },
      "candidate_status": "task_ambiguous",
      "authorization_source": false
    },
    {
      "id": "n0028",
      "kind": "INSTR_ACTION",
      "operation": "file.write",
      "resource": "unknown",
      "summary": "4. If an export cannot be re-framed (vendor mesh, scanned part), a nonzero visual origin is acceptable but must be recorded in the ledger with its source; it is a per-link constant, not a tuning knob.",
      "provenance": {
        "file": "references/meshes.md",
        "line_start": 12,
        "line_end": 12
      },
      "candidate_status": "task_ambiguous",
      "authorization_source": false
    },
